<title>USA: Caterpillar debt rating raised.</title>
<headline>Caterpillar debt rating raised.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-07-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Duff &amp; Phelps Credit Rating Co said it raised its rating on the senior unsecured debt of Caterpillar Inc to single-A-plus from single-A.</p>
<p>The credit rating agency also said it affirmed the heavy equipment maker's commercial paper rating at D-one.</p>
<p>&quot;The rating change reflects Caterpillar's success in expanding margins, the superior market positions achieved by its diverse product line, strong cash flow in comparison with financial obligations and reinvestment requirements and attractive growth prospects,&quot; Duff &amp; Phelps said.</p>
<p>((--Chicago Newsdesk 312-408-8787))</p>
</text>
